course: dictionary
lesson: 3644
title: Firebox and the steam engine
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words come from old machines, and you may not meet them every day. Context helps. «A fireman shovelled coal into the firebox.» Shovelled means pushed with a shovel, and coal is fuel that burns, so the firebox must be the place where the fire burns.
explain: Look at the word itself. Firebox is made of two smaller words, fire and box, joined together. Many English words work this way, so spotting the parts can help you guess a meaning.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence: «A fireman shovelled coal into the part of the engine where the fire burns.» It still makes sense, so you have the right idea.
fact: Firebox means the part of a steam engine, boiler or stove where the fire burns.
fact: In a steam train, the fire in the firebox heats water and makes steam.
fact: «Firebox» is a compound word: «fire» and «box» joined together.
fact: In The Wind in the Willows, Toad helps the engine driver by feeding the furnace, which is the firebox, with coal.
fact: In an old US meaning, a firebox was a box on a street with an alarm to call firefighters.
exercise: «A fireman shovelled coal into the firebox.» What does firebox mean? | A tool for pushing coal | A box of matches for lighting the fire | A driver's seat at the front of the train | *The part of an engine where the fire burns
exercise: In a steam train, what does the fire in the firebox heat? | *Water, to make steam | Snow on the tracks | The passengers' tickets | The guard's whistle
exercise: Which word is made of two smaller words joined together? | whistle | steam | driver | *firebox
test: «Toad helped the driver by feeding the firebox with coal.» What did Toad feed into the firebox? | *Coal | Water from a bucket | A whistle | A flag
test: In The Wind in the Willows, which word means the same as firebox in «feeding the furnace with coal»? | Whistle | *Firebox | Guard | Driver
exam: «A steam engine had a driver and a fireman, who shovelled coal into the firebox.» What was the fireman's job? | *To shovel coal into the firebox | To sell tickets to the passengers | To wave a flag and blow a whistle | To drive the train from the front
